// cscript JScript (Node is blocked), the l4b-2a unit-harness pattern: every function under test is
// EXTRACTED BY TEXT from the real bytes of js/views.js and js/state.js and run in one scope against a
// stubbed state and a small fake DOM (createElement / appendChild / setAttribute / addEventListener;
// textContent and innerHTML are plain properties, so every innerHTML the page writes is visible to the
// scan). Against a tree without the category page (HEAD 096269a) it refuses to load: exit 2.
//   C1  cpRoomRoute / cpFromLabel / cpHash / cpLabelOf (every category round-trips; bad labels refused)
//   C2  the head: counts line (read = read + finished only), lens rows (order, other reader, none shared),
//       notes (newest first, Journal never, another reader never)
//   C3  the grid: 6 / 7 at 390; 8 / 12 from 1000
//   C4  "+ N more" and "See all N" open in place and survive a same-route re-render
//   C5  page state resets on arrival from another route and on a category change
//   C6  text never reaches markup: a title / author / lens name / note body carrying HTML
//   C7  the empty state: unknown, script-bearing and malformed labels; a category with none of mine
//   C8  the route branch: bare #category -> #books; a label renders
//   C9  Back and the tab: from the Shelf, You, Home, Search; a lens / book / note opened from the page
//   C10 the doors: the Shelf band name (category / lens / other) and lxOrbOpen; the orb copy
//   C11 signed out: the Shelf's own words
//   C12 writes: books / userBooks / userThemes / notebookEntries byte-identical after every step,
//       no ls / sv call; ensureLensLooks once per signed-in render (the fold)
//   C13 a cover whose image fails draws its title and author instead (red-team R1, folded in)
// EXTENSIONLESS on purpose (see tools/parse-check). ASCII-only: cscript reads it as ANSI, so the page's
// middle dot arrives as two characters; texts are compared with every non-ASCII run folded to "|".
//
// Usage:  cscript //nologo //E:jscript docs/checkpoints/l4b-2b-shots/unit-harness [root]
// Exit:   0 = every case passed . 1 = a case failed . 2 = could not load

